#lang rzk-1

-- A plain contradiction is NOT visible under a _b lock, so `mod _b recBOT` over a
-- plain contradiction must be rejected. Keeping the plain tope under the lock
-- would need the unit id => _b (phi |- _b phi); but _b is comonadic (counit
-- _b A |- A only) and has no such unit -- that is _#, the monad -- so plain topes
-- are dropped under a _b lock (coe Id Flat = False) and the locked context is no
-- longer contradictory. (Without the lock, `\ _ -> recBOT : ... -> _b A`
-- typechecks by plain ex falso.)
#def ill-recBOT-under-flat
  (A :_b U) (i : 2)
  : (i : 2 | (i === 0_2) /\ (i === 1_2)) -> _b A
  := \ _ -> mod _b recBOT
